Let's write functions.

`expand_targets`:
```
sub expand_targets {
 my @specs=@_;
 my @targets; my %seen;
 for my $spec (@specs) {
   next empty
   if ($spec =~ /^(\d+)\.(\d+)\.(\d+)\.(\d+)\/(\d+)$/) { validate; ... }
   elsif ($spec =~ /^([a-zA-Z0-9._-]+)$/) { key lc; }
   else error and exit1
 }
 return @targets;
}
```
CIDR expansion:
```
my $base = ($a<<24)|...
my $count=1<<(32-prefix)
for my $i...
 if prefix <=30 && ($i==0||$i==$count-1) skip
 push unless seen
 die if @targets > max
```
Need support input `/24` and 500 count. For /31 include. /32 include.
Could target `10.0.0.1/32`. good.
